{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "25 feels like a natural next choice because its expressive singing and emotional ballads fit my interest in polished vocal performances on Stages and Lead With Your Heart.",
    "Eagles: The Very Best Of appeals because its melodic songs connect with the country and vocal-focused listening in my history; the Beatles selections also capture some of that tunefulness."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Appetite For Destruction, Master of Puppets, and A Different Kind of Truth emphasize aggressive guitars and intensity, while I currently want soothing music or prominent, polished singing.",
    "Fallen feels too heavy and dark, and Kid A's experimental textures do not offer the clear melodies and vocal focus that make the other choices appealing to me."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in some older songs seems to have been stretched into an interest in classic rock generally, even though melody and mood matter more to me than an album's era.",
    "My listening to country and pop seems to have been treated as a broad appetite for guitar-based music, overlooking the difference between gentle, melodic songs and forceful hard rock."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent choice, The Most Relaxing Classical Music in the Universe, suggests that a calm listening experience deserves more weight right now.",
    "My repeated choices of vocal-focused albums suggest that expressive voices and polished arrangements matter more than simply offering familiar songs; that is why I would choose 25 before the Beatles compilations today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my taste for melody and expressive singing but stretched it too far toward heavy and experimental music."
}"}
